WEBVTT

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:19.290
See you later.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:37.120
I can, too...

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:51.440
The Current Buzz! Idols to Watch Out For!

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:51.490
LizNoir, the hottest idol group
among young women right now,

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:54.620
just announced the release
of their new single.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:59.660
Don't miss Rio Kanzaki and Aoi Igawa
shine in their new music video.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.740
Morning, Kotono!

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.290
Morning.

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.120
Morning, Kotono.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.660
Would you like scrambled eggs or an omelet?

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.160
Um...

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.620
Hey, you two, did you take out the trash yet?

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.700
S-Suzu and Shizuku,

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.450
let's wake up now.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:15.910
Give two more hours...

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:17.290
Seconded...

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:18.410
What...?

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.790
Come on!

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:23.700
There's a delicious meal waiting for you!

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.450
Go wash your face...

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.330
...and get changed!

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.790
Chisa, where is my uniform?

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.660
Suzu, don't undress here!

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:34.540
So...

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.040
What's your preference?

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.040
Chore Chart

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.450
What everyone else likes.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.460
"Hoshimi High School"

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:16.040
I see...

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.410
That sounds lively and fun.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:19.870
I don't know.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:24.120
We sometimes argue over
Miss Saki's nit-picky rules.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:27.040
What do you do when that happens, Kotono?

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.410
Huh?

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:33.080
"I'm fine either way."

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.830
"I'll follow what everyone decides on."

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.040
Spot on?

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.490
Not at all.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:41.370
You're all a group, right?

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.240
You all have to get along!

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.540
You know me.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.370
I'm not good at that kind of thing.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:53.040
Well, you've gathered quite a group with
a diverse range of skills and characters.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.790
I really hope they work out together.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:59.660
It's our job to help them achieve that, right?

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.450
A group is all about balance.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:05.290
If anything is off, it can collapse any moment.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:06.490
Yes.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:10.240
Excuse me.

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:11.490
Is Makino available?

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:13.740
That's "Mr. Makino," to you.

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:15.580
Or call me "Manager."

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:18.410
So, why is everyone gathered here?

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:21.660
We've finished our core
and vocal training for the day.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:22.620
And so...

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:26.370
I am sick of basic training every single day!

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:30.200
It's about time we start practicing
choreography or do a recording!

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:34.240
Well... How can we record
when we don't even have a song?

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.790
That's what I said, too.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:40.490
But I can understand
where Suzu is coming from.

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:42.330
Yes, basic training is important,

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:46.290
but doing it so long without trainers
or a goal makes us anxious.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:48.120
That's true.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.120
You've got a point there.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:53.160
So, we actually talked about it...

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:57.910
And we're wondering if we could practice
choreography of an easy song.

00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:00.160
Would that be a problem?

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:02.740
I think it's fine.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:06.120
Basic training is a drag
when there's no motivation.

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:08.200
I get that, but...

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:12.580
It's your job to get the girls
excited, right, Makino?

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:15.160
You say that like people won't misinterpret it.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:16.620
What do you mean?

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.660
Oh, nothing.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:21.950
I want to make sure this
is everyone's request.

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:23.540
Shizuku? Chisa?

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:25.160
Yup.

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:28.790
I'm not too confident, but I'll do my best.

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:31.040
How about you, Kotono?

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.540
I...

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:36.410
As long as I can start real lessons,
I'm fine with it.

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:37.950
I see.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:41.200
All right, then I'll find a song
to work on by tomorrow.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:44.120
All right!

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:44.120
--This is so great!
--Yup!

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.080
Let's do our best, Kotono!

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.080
--We did it!
--Yeah!

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.370
Y-Yeah...

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.370
Now we've got singing
and dancing to work on!

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.790
As expected of Makino.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:57.240
The manager who chose me
as the center idol!

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:59.120
He really gets it.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:01.790
What? Suzu, you're the center idol?

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:05.200
Well of course! I am <i>the</i> daughter
of the prestigious Narumiya family.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:07.660
Our name is known to everyone in Hoshimi City.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.540
O-Oh, I see...

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:13.490
I think we can be a fun group with you, Suzu.

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:15.660
That is right, indeed!

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:17.080
Hey!

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:20.620
How about we go out to eat
as a celebration tonight?

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:22.160
Splendid idea!

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.700
What is the dress code for that establishment?

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:28.200
What? I don't think it would be
that kind of place...

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.160
Miss Saki, what do you think?

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.660
Well, as long as we don't get home too late...

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:37.540
And I actually have lots to say to everyone.

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:41.160
Be quiet at night.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.740
Put away your dirty clothes.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:46.540
You'll oversleep again
if you don't go to bed now.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:53.040
So it's set. Let's go, Kotono!

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:53.910
Yeah?

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:55.660
Sorry.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:57.120
I still have things to do.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.370
Things to do?

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:02.200
You all have fun.

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:03.120
Bye.

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:05.450
Hey!

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:09.290
There she goes.

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:10.410
Yes...

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.490
It's hamburg steak tonight!

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:16.620
Wow, yay!

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.080
Don't you know the curry flavor is better?

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.740
Leave me alone.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:23.790
This is my dinner.

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:29.040
It's Kotono.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:32.160
Good evening.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.540
Hey!

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:35.740
What was that?

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:37.830
Oh... It's nothing.

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:41.660
Kotono... Late training today?

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:42.870
Yes.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:45.490
I see.

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:50.040
If you get back too late,
you'll get everyone worried.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:51.120
Mr. Makino.

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:55.080
Why does it have to be a group?

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:04.870
You do know that the Venus Program's
top-ranking idols are groups, right?

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:08.330
But my sister was a solo artist.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:12.740
Well, I consider her as a sort of miracle.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:16.290
I've come to understand after
three years of trial and error.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:18.620
In order to satisfy the audience,

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:22.540
you can't just be good at singing or dancing.

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:26.870
You can't survive in today's program
with just a unique character, either.

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:30.450
That's why I needed a
diverse range of characters.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:31.950
Character...?

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:33.950
It hasn't come together yet,

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:38.620
but eventually everyone's characters will
blend together and become a great appeal.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:40.450
That's what I believe.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.330
Still not satisfied?

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:44.950
To be honest...

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:47.450
I still don't understand.

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:48.700
But...

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:54.200
I'll be okay as long as I can stand on
the stage my sister dreamed about.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:59.450
Well, if you want a great concert,
you'll eventually need to talk to everyone.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:00.790
I know.

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:01.950
All right.

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:05.370
Then I'm counting on you to take care of
our new member who starts tomorrow.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:05.850
What?

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:07.950
It might surprise you.

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:09.020
Especially since she's--

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:10.990
I-I'm going to jog home!

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:12.330
Hey!

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:14.580
I'll get to meet her tomorrow!

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:20.450
Well... We all can't change overnight.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.870
Hoshimi Productions

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:26.120
What?

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:29.490
I'm Nagisa Ibuki. A second-year at Hoshimi High.

00:09:29.490 --> 00:09:31.490
It's very nice to meet you all.

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:32.870
Nagisa?!

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:33.870
But why?!

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:38.200
I secretly applied to this
agency when you did, too.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:39.330
Is she a friend?

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:40.870
Y-Yeah.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:43.450
Are you Sakura?

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:44.540
Yes.

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:47.120
Kotono talks about you all the time.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:48.700
I see.

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:52.990
She was wrong about you
when she first met you,

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:54.620
so she felt really bad.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:55.790
What?

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:58.990
She couldn't understand your
reasoning to become an idol,

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:02.290
but she's impressed at how you take on
the lessons more seriously than anyone.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:05.490
She's been wanting to apologize for a while now.

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:06.410
Nagisa!

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.660
I knew you hadn't told her yet!

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:11.950
It's better to communicate
these things, you know?

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:14.200
That's how you get closer!

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:19.080
I've never seen Kotono make
that kind of face before.

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:21.870
Yeah, it's a bit surprising.

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:24.660
All right, let's start with the basics as usual.

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:27.120
I'll announce the song after that.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:28.370
Yes!

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:34.790
Not fair.

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:36.120
Not fair?

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:39.200
You could've told me Nagisa was joining.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.410
Actually, you're the one
who left when I was about to.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:44.870
Kotono!

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.790
Let's do some stretches together.

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.490
Y-Yeah!

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:55.790
<i>Idoly Pride.</i>

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:00.450
And now, in celebration of
Nagisa joining the group...

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:02.490
Cheers!

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:09.830
I never expected you to be interested
in becoming an idol, Nagisa.

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:12.740
I would see you working hard

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:15.660
and it made me want to try, too!

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:17.160
Does it bother you?

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:18.490
Not at all.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:21.870
To be honest, I was feeling a little lonely.

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:22.830
So thank you.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:26.580
Hey Suzu, so why do you
want to become an idol?

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.660
Huh? M-Me?

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.160
Yeah.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:32.120
Everyone else, too.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.410
Right, Kotono?

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:34.370
Huh?

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:36.580
We'll be working together as a team now,

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:38.830
so let's get to know each other better.

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:40.290
Right...

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:43.580
Well,

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:46.830
I thought it would be a breeze
for me to get to the top.

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.950
I've always loved idols.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:51.160
Chisa, you too, right?

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:52.870
Y-Yeah.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:56.370
I knew my sister would pass the audition,

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:59.490
but I don't know why I did.

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:03.120
I wonder if I passed as a backup idol.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:05.240
Did I just trigger something?

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:07.950
How about you, Sakura?

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:09.700
I'm here because...

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:12.200
My heart pounded really fast!

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:17.240
Um... I do not understand.

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:20.910
So... It was some sort of fate, maybe?

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:24.120
How about you, Shizuku?

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:26.620
Because I... love idols.

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:28.080
So the same as us.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.290
Yup.

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:32.700
So... Um...

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:35.160
Care to tell us?

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:36.580
Me?

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:41.660
I want to stand at the top of
the Venus Program for my sister.

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:43.830
That's my goal.

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:45.040
Your sister?!

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:46.540
Nagase?!

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:49.080
Could... your sister be...?!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:51.490
What? It's Miss Mana, right?

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:52.740
So it is!

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:54.120
Late, much?

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:56.540
I see, for your sister...

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:57.910
Is that bad?

00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:00.740
No, I'm very moved.

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:04.540
How Miss Mana's spirit is being kept alive.

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:07.290
Miss Mana was an amazing idol.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:09.830
Miss Mana was that amazing?

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:13.240
How could you say such a thing!

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:15.580
Who do you think Miss Mana is?!

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:16.950
She is <i>the</i> Miss Mana!

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:22.370
Known as the miraculous star idol
who put Hoshimi City on the map!

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:26.290
Her video became one of the top ten
most watched in Japan within a year!

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:29.160
The Next Venus Grand Prix
was just a passage point.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:33.330
She was eventually set to stand
at the pinnacle of idols.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:37.370
You all have no idea how hard it was,
even for me, to acquire her autograph!

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.080
Stay right there!

